    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 14 tests across Cp01\u2013Cp07, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe spec: **when no registration date is supplied, default it to the server's current date, and return `registrationDate` in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.** The one endpoint under test is `POST /api/owners`, read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, this makes the field both accepted on create and returned on read. `format: date` generates a `LocalDate` in the DTOs and serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`, matching the existing `birthDate` convention.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (model) \u2014 added a persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after mapping the request, if `registrationDate` is null it defaults to `LocalDate.now()`; a supplied date is left untouched.\n\n4. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. The test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column has to exist in `schema.sql`.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps `registrationDate` automatically in both directions (matching property names), so no mapper change was needed. `updateOwner` sets individual fields and doesn't touch `registrationDate`, so it's preserved across updates.\n\nBoth new checkpoint tests pass: `coreDefaultsToToday` (omitted \u2192 today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (supplied `2020-06-15` round-trips).",
